WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:08.760
My name is Katarzyna Żeglicka.

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:14.160
I'm a feminist and queer activist
from Poland.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:21.720
I'm also a performer, choreographer
and Wendo trainer -

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.280
assertiveness and self-defense
training for women and girls.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:39.400
I'd define my art as the
art of resistance.

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:46.400
I like to say that it is activism
through dance.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:01:02.913
A very important part of my life 
with movement

00:01:02.913 --> 00:01:07.320
was the dance study
"Resonance of Contrast".

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:17.120
The show was presented on a medical chair,
which was a very important decision in this performance.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:24.912
I sat on it and tried to show
the experiences of women

00:01:24.912 --> 00:01:30.520
in contact with medical institutions.

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:41.515
The next layer of the performance
was a film with my eyes

00:01:41.515 --> 00:01:48.320
with nystagmus
displayed in front of the audience.

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:53.880
So, again, I tried to provoke people
watching me, but also myself to look

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:56.400
at my non-normative eyes 
that are constantly in motion.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:03.720
The whole performance lasts 10 minutes
and the whole study was through me

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:09.240
as if I was dancing 
to the sound of an MRI scan.

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:16.565
I wanted to show how the contrast that I am,

00:02:16.565 --> 00:02:22.400
which is in my eyes and in my gaze, 
resonates with the viewer,

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:31.920
but also how I resonate
with Polish violent institutions.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:41.360
For me, creating, moving, dancing,

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:44.520
it creates a sense of freedom
and independence

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:49.920
but also a form of opposition and resistance,
a form of shouting and anger.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:59.120
I'm at a moment where I'm trying to confront
viewers with how I live

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:04.120
with an impairment and a non-normative body.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:08.880
I try to put people who are watching me
in a slightly uncomfortable position

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:14.240
and confront them with what is happening
to me somehow,

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:16.600
with what happens to me in life.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:21.440
However, I don't treat my art as therapy,

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:30.280
it is more a form of disagreement, resistance to
what happens to disabled women.

